WEBVTT

00:02.752 --> 00:06.732
<i>The new lord of Kasdeks Domain...</i>

00:08.252 --> 00:12.402
He's said to have many 
female slaves attend him.

00:14.152 --> 00:17.712
<i>I'm not letting a guy like that 
anywhere near Iluk Village.</i>

00:18.712 --> 00:22.452
That man with the belly like 
a barrel is a strong blue.

00:22.942 --> 00:23.722
What?

00:23.722 --> 00:27.482
Not as intense at yours, 
but it's still pretty strong.

00:27.482 --> 00:29.712
No one accompanying him is red.

00:34.602 --> 00:37.222
My sincerest apologies! Do forgive me!

00:37.572 --> 00:42.562
I just had to meet the man
I so admire for myself, Lord Dias!

00:43.002 --> 00:45.562
My name is Eldan Kasdeks.

00:45.562 --> 00:47.992
You can simply call me Eldan!

02:20.032 --> 02:22.652
Ever since I was a child, 
I've had the utmost respect

02:22.652 --> 02:25.772
for the kingdom's
 heroic savior, Lord Dias!

02:25.772 --> 02:29.292
And I got it in my head that 
we should be on good terms.

02:29.802 --> 02:33.552
I promise not to do wrong by you, 
so I hope you aren't upset.

02:35.402 --> 02:39.052
It's not that I'm upset, Lord Eldan...

02:39.292 --> 02:45.052
And I apologize as well for my 
rude treatment of Mr. Kamalotz.

02:45.412 --> 02:48.002
No need to fret over rudeness!

02:48.002 --> 02:50.682
You're more than welcome
 to dispense with formalities with us!

02:51.132 --> 02:55.312
By the way, Lord Dias, who might 
the young woman next to you be?

02:57.332 --> 03:01.392
I must say, she's very good at hiding.

03:01.972 --> 03:05.322
But my ears and nose are keen, 
so I know she's there.

03:05.992 --> 03:10.332
She has a nice, kind scent,
 just as you do.

03:11.202 --> 03:14.082
<i>Concealment doesn't work with him?!</i>

03:23.452 --> 03:25.962
Who are your people, miss?

03:25.962 --> 03:28.562
What is your relationship with Lord Dias?!

03:28.972 --> 03:32.692
Her name is Alna, and she's my fian—

03:31.602 --> 03:33.112
Wife!

03:32.332 --> 03:33.582
<b>WIFE</b>

03:34.562 --> 03:36.562
I'm his wife.

03:38.502 --> 03:39.322
Yeah.

03:39.842 --> 03:41.502
That horn...

03:41.502 --> 03:43.572
Are you a demihuman, Miss Alna?

03:43.832 --> 03:47.612
I'm an onikin, and I was 
born with this horn.

03:47.612 --> 03:51.162
I've never heard the word "demihuman," 
so I do not know how to answer.

03:51.542 --> 03:57.072
Demihuman is a general term for peoples 
that aren't human but are similar to them,

03:57.072 --> 03:59.972
such as beastkin and fishkin.

04:01.082 --> 04:03.802
Then I guess you could say
 I'm a demihuman.

04:10.302 --> 04:12.152
Lord Dias!

04:12.152 --> 04:16.352
Have you had a child with Miss Alna?!

04:15.162 --> 04:17.652
Whoa, whoa, whoa! Why are you crying?!

04:17.882 --> 04:20.402
Get a hold of yourself!
We don't have any children!

04:21.202 --> 04:23.652
I plan to have ten of them.

04:23.962 --> 04:24.972
Alna?!

04:25.682 --> 04:28.602
We don't have any children of our own yet,

04:28.602 --> 04:32.192
but Dias is raising two orphans 
who appear to be demihumans.

04:33.142 --> 04:37.672
Lord Dias has a demihuman wife 
and demihuman children?!

04:46.252 --> 04:50.182
Mother! I've found a comrade!

04:50.182 --> 04:55.762
And it's none other than Lord Dias!

04:53.182 --> 04:54.062
Dias!

04:54.412 --> 04:57.702
Don't tell me... You're a demihuman, too?

05:00.412 --> 05:01.072
What's wrong?!

05:01.662 --> 05:02.512
Are you okay?!

05:13.392 --> 05:16.842
What in the world is going on with him?

05:19.602 --> 05:21.882
I don't mind if you tell him.

05:23.332 --> 05:24.332
Yes, milord.

05:24.922 --> 05:31.502
Lord Eldan is a half-demihuman, 
born to a demihuman and a human.

05:31.502 --> 05:38.252
He can assume either form, 
but the shift between is quite taxing.

05:39.582 --> 05:45.232
Half-demihumans are rare, and being 
one is an advantage for Lord Eldan.

05:45.562 --> 05:52.742
However, not having a single stable 
form does pose its difficulties.

05:52.742 --> 05:58.252
This is why he cannot do 
without the devoted care of his wives.

05:58.872 --> 06:01.242
I was so delighted earlier,

06:01.242 --> 06:04.662
in my excitement, 
I changed form in spite of myself.

06:04.662 --> 06:06.262
My apologies.

06:06.522 --> 06:08.202
Don't worry about it.

06:08.202 --> 06:10.762
Now then, I understand
 there's been a rebellion...

06:12.242 --> 06:16.772
That was to protect those dear to me.

06:17.222 --> 06:22.522
It all began when Lord Eldan was born.

06:23.222 --> 06:27.282
The previous lord, Lord Enkars, 
already had a wife and son,

06:27.282 --> 06:31.412
but his eldest son's personality 
was just as hideous as his.

06:31.782 --> 06:35.412
Enkars alienated this son, 
who was so similar to himself,

06:35.412 --> 06:41.172
while he was highly fond of his bright,
handsome son born to an elephantkin slave.

06:41.502 --> 06:47.172
The lord declared him his true son,
awarding the boy position and authority.

06:47.172 --> 06:49.902
That son was Lord Eldan.

06:49.902 --> 06:55.182
Until I was five years old, 
I thought I was a regular human.

06:55.742 --> 06:59.682
But a chance occurrence 
revealed the real me,

07:00.212 --> 07:04.682
and I learned that my true 
mother was kept as a slave.

07:04.682 --> 07:10.192
Starting then, Lord Eldan secretly 
got to know his mother better,

07:10.992 --> 07:14.952
and he worked behind the scenes 
to safeguard demihumans,

07:15.432 --> 07:19.882
all while keeping this from Enkars, 
who would sooner have them in chains.

07:20.862 --> 07:26.212
I want to make a world where everyone can 
live in happiness, whoever their people.

07:26.662 --> 07:28.882
That is what I wish for!

07:31.472 --> 07:36.942
His wives were all slaves, 
but Lord Eldan saved them.

07:36.942 --> 07:42.982
Inspired by his ideals, they've chosen
 to become his caretakers.

07:44.552 --> 07:47.732
Then what of all the talk
 about the lord's second son

07:47.732 --> 07:50.232
being attended by a bevy
 of enslaved women?

07:50.692 --> 07:56.672
That was a rumor we spread 
intentionally, but in fact,

07:56.672 --> 08:02.002
Lord Eldan and his wives love 
each other with all their hearts.

08:06.912 --> 08:10.632
However, the deception was 
not easy to maintain.

08:11.362 --> 08:15.132
Enkars was enraged when he learned 
of Lord Eldan's true goal.

08:15.402 --> 08:18.982
He declared he would put every last 
demihuman in the domain to death,

08:18.982 --> 08:21.592
including Lord Eldan and his mother.

08:22.142 --> 08:25.892
Lord Eldan raised an army 
to protect the demihumans.

08:25.892 --> 08:29.962
After a hard-fought conflict, 
he defeated Enkars's forces.

08:31.722 --> 08:33.072
<i>I see now.</i>

08:33.072 --> 08:37.162
<i>That's what he meant about 
protecting those dear to him.</i>

08:37.482 --> 08:42.682
I apologize for forgetting myself
in my excitement earlier.

08:42.682 --> 08:46.952
When I heard the hero I admire 
has a demihuman family,

08:46.952 --> 08:49.932
I thought you must be a kindred 
spirit with the same dream.

08:51.802 --> 08:54.862
So... there's just one thing 
I'd like to confirm.

08:54.862 --> 08:58.922
When you say "the hero you 
admire," do you mean me?

08:58.922 --> 09:01.432
Who else would I mean?

09:01.432 --> 09:06.942
Tales of Sir Dias, heroic savior of the 
kingdom, have made their way to Kasdeks.

09:07.172 --> 09:11.312
He upholds his parents' dying 
wishes, rescues the weak,

09:11.312 --> 09:13.072
cuts down thousands of foes,

09:13.072 --> 09:15.942
and uses his fists to persuade 
tyrannical nobles to reform.

09:15.942 --> 09:17.942
I hear the heroic saga of Lord Dias

09:17.942 --> 09:22.402
has even been performed 
as a stage play in the capital

09:22.402 --> 09:24.952
to lift morale and 
recruit volunteer soldiers.

09:27.092 --> 09:29.142
Apparently, public performances
 were suspended

09:29.142 --> 09:31.112
as soon as the aristocracy intervened.

09:31.112 --> 09:35.462
But the tales spread by word of mouth, 
and now everyone knows your story.

09:35.692 --> 09:38.102
<i>This is the first I've heard of it.</i>

09:38.432 --> 09:41.972
<i>I bet the bulk of it is entirely made up.</i>

09:42.362 --> 09:45.182
I don't believe every 
single thing I've heard,

09:45.182 --> 09:49.652
but returning soldiers talk, 
and your reputation proceeds you.

09:49.652 --> 09:53.232
And now that I've met you, 
I'd say you exceed the tales.

09:53.752 --> 09:57.262
Of course he does. He's my husband.

09:59.382 --> 10:02.932
And so I ask you again, Lord Dias...

10:02.932 --> 10:05.372
I hope we can be on good terms.

10:05.772 --> 10:07.902
That we can work toward a world where

10:07.902 --> 10:10.312
demihumans and humans 
live together in harmony.

10:10.622 --> 10:12.632
It's my dream!

10:16.932 --> 10:17.762
Eldan.

10:19.132 --> 10:21.402
I support that dream.

10:21.732 --> 10:27.182
In my village, humans and demihumans 
already coexist in peace.

10:27.712 --> 10:33.152
I, too, think it would be good 
to see that in more places.

10:34.802 --> 10:36.612
So I ask you in turn...

10:36.612 --> 10:39.252
I'd very much like you and
 your people to be our friends.

10:43.232 --> 10:47.212
Eldan, your ideals are truly commendable.

10:47.212 --> 10:50.892
I think you can afford to take more
 pride in them. Don't be ashamed.

11:08.262 --> 11:13.442
Good. Now we each have a grasp 
on the state of the other's domain.

11:13.802 --> 11:15.602
About finding more subjects...

11:15.602 --> 11:18.892
I asked a traveling merchant 
the other day to spread the word,

11:18.892 --> 11:21.652
but do you have any other suggestions?

11:21.652 --> 11:24.452
I will make a proclamation 
in Kasdeks as well.

11:24.872 --> 11:28.022
But there's something you should do first.

11:28.702 --> 11:32.712
I think you'll be in trouble 
if you don't amass larger food stores.

11:32.712 --> 11:34.882
You must begin producing
 within your domain,

11:34.882 --> 11:37.712
especially if you plan 
to have more subjects.

11:38.742 --> 11:41.442
Winter seems far away, 
but it sneaks up on you.

11:41.442 --> 11:45.262
If you don't prepare now, 
you will come to regret it later.

11:45.712 --> 11:48.972
Understood. Thank you for the sage advice.

11:49.542 --> 11:52.452
I plan to be as helpful as possible.

11:55.122 --> 11:57.222
See you next time, Eldan!

11:57.222 --> 12:00.672
I look forward to it!

12:09.542 --> 12:10.372
We're home.

12:11.242 --> 12:13.452
You said you'd be right back!

12:13.452 --> 12:14.622
We waited for you!

12:14.622 --> 12:16.132
Dias, you liar!

12:16.132 --> 12:18.152
You tricked us!

12:19.712 --> 12:22.132
I-I'm sorry.

12:25.552 --> 12:27.662
They finally fell asleep.

12:27.662 --> 12:30.322
And they look happy enough now.

12:31.022 --> 12:33.862
After that huge tantrum, too.

12:33.862 --> 12:35.772
That's how kids are.

12:36.052 --> 12:41.022
But Dias, are you sure that
you shouldn't have scolded them?

12:41.292 --> 12:43.732
They hit, they kicked,

12:43.732 --> 12:46.832
and they even insisted on staying 
up late because "you lied!"

12:46.832 --> 12:48.912
Isn't that bad behavior?

12:48.912 --> 12:53.952
I don't suppose it's good, 
but I'm the one who broke a promise,

12:53.952 --> 12:55.912
and I wanted to start by apologizing.

12:56.722 --> 12:59.032
It's common for children 
who just joined a family

12:59.032 --> 13:04.262
to speak willfully and be wild 
in order to test the adults.

13:04.782 --> 13:06.772
I'll allow it for now.

13:07.222 --> 13:12.252
But if it continues, 
they're not growing up right.

13:12.572 --> 13:15.772
I intend to set them straight 
if they keep it up tomorrow.

13:18.832 --> 13:23.952
By the way, about food production
as Eldan pointed out...

13:23.952 --> 13:24.782
Yes.

13:25.202 --> 13:27.832
I think I'll start by cultivating a field.

13:28.672 --> 13:33.202
I did lots of farmwork before the war, 
so I like to think I'm used to it.

13:33.202 --> 13:36.092
Say, Dias, around here, fields...

13:38.902 --> 13:41.542
Intruders. Quite a few of them.

13:42.152 --> 13:44.782
Are you sure it's not Eldan's people?

13:44.782 --> 13:47.642
They're coming from a different direction
than the way Eldan left.

13:47.642 --> 13:52.052
Besides, would anyone respectable 
be wandering around at this hour?

13:52.052 --> 13:55.112
In that case, it must be bandits.

13:55.112 --> 13:56.772
That's not good news.

13:57.032 --> 13:59.332
It's late. I'll go take a look.

13:59.332 --> 14:00.792
You stay here—

13:59.902 --> 14:01.662
I'm going, too.

14:02.412 --> 14:04.022
Tonight is the new moon.

14:04.452 --> 14:08.482
How could you possibly find 
them without any help?

14:08.482 --> 14:11.782
Meaning you're going to need my magic.

14:12.222 --> 14:14.482
Let Klaus hold the fort.

14:17.062 --> 14:19.042
I could swear someone just said my name.

14:22.202 --> 14:24.792
Take me with you, Dias.

14:27.452 --> 14:28.302
All right.

14:29.072 --> 14:31.402
Lend me a hand, Alna.

14:32.052 --> 14:37.062
<b>THE FRONTIER LORD AND THE NEIGHBORING LORD</b>

14:43.812 --> 14:47.422
Are there really any humans out here?

14:47.762 --> 14:49.822
I ain't even seen a single tree around.

14:50.172 --> 14:51.822
We're going the right way.

14:52.072 --> 14:55.372
I spent a fortune hiring you guys.

14:55.372 --> 14:58.792
If you're only good for running 
your mouth, return my money.

14:59.032 --> 15:02.602
Oh, no, we'll do the job right.

15:02.602 --> 15:06.042
But why now, on a night with no moon?

15:06.472 --> 15:09.802
Have you not heard of Dias, 
the kingdom's heroic savior?

15:10.502 --> 15:13.732
You'd never beat him head-on
 in broad daylight.

15:13.732 --> 15:16.202
Fail to take him by surprise
and you won't stand a chance.

15:16.902 --> 15:21.442
Tall tales like that 
are just a buncha talk.

15:21.442 --> 15:26.592
Besides, there's no possible way 
we'd lose with this many fighters.

15:26.592 --> 15:28.372
Don't talk back to me!

15:28.372 --> 15:31.972
And if you find that Eldan guy, 
kill him, too!

15:31.972 --> 15:34.072
He's a young fellow with a potbelly.

15:34.072 --> 15:37.022
For a little extra, you mean?

15:37.922 --> 15:40.192
A hundred silver coins for Eldan,

15:40.192 --> 15:44.082
and if you kill Dias, 
you'll get a bonus of ten gold coins.

15:44.082 --> 15:45.512
Oho!

15:45.512 --> 15:50.592
Okay, boys, get ready! 
It's our first big score in a while!

15:50.592 --> 15:52.592
Yeah!

15:52.592 --> 15:55.932
Let's get this over with 
and head back to town!

15:58.182 --> 16:00.932
Boss! Lyle's been hit!

15:58.182 --> 15:59.932
Ow!

16:03.102 --> 16:04.462
Ditch the torches!

16:04.462 --> 16:06.712
Fire back at that red light!

16:10.342 --> 16:11.562
<i>It went out?</i>

16:11.562 --> 16:13.592
<i>What was that light?</i>

16:14.902 --> 16:18.482
<i>That's way too accurate 
for so few shots fired.</i>

16:18.482 --> 16:21.182
<i>How can they tell where we are?</i>

16:22.162 --> 16:23.782
Keep firing bolts and arrows!

16:23.782 --> 16:25.692
We can win with numbers 
if they've made us!

16:25.942 --> 16:27.972
Fire away and smoke 'em out!

16:29.562 --> 16:30.302
You okay?!

16:31.172 --> 16:35.392
I heard voices! Thataway! Surround 'em!

16:36.202 --> 16:38.062
Payback time, asshole.

16:38.062 --> 16:39.432
We're gonna kill you!

16:42.332 --> 16:42.932
What?!

16:46.852 --> 16:49.022
It's not just an archer!

16:49.022 --> 16:50.192
Get into formation!

16:50.442 --> 16:51.212
Yessir!

16:54.062 --> 16:56.492
<i>Four guys in the blink of an eye?</i>

16:58.222 --> 17:01.742
<i>N-Now there's a green light? 
Could it be a demihuman?!</i>

17:02.472 --> 17:03.542
Damn it!

17:03.542 --> 17:07.082
Where are you?! 
Get out here, you monsters!

17:10.962 --> 17:15.972
<i>Blue eyes, steel armor, 
a big two-handed axe...</i>

17:16.432 --> 17:17.222
<i>He must be...</i>

17:18.972 --> 17:19.802
<i>Son of a...</i>

17:20.332 --> 17:24.552
<i>Even a hundred gold coins 
ain't enough for a monster like him!</i>

17:27.592 --> 17:29.582
Shit! Shit, shit!

17:30.012 --> 17:31.462
Useless, the lot of them!

17:31.462 --> 17:33.842
I <i>told</i> them we were doomed
 if were made!

17:47.382 --> 17:51.332
Ow! My old wound's acting up.

17:53.202 --> 17:56.412
This is all your fault, Dias!

17:56.932 --> 18:00.912
It was my due right as a noble!

18:00.912 --> 18:02.802
And yet he dared to...

18:02.802 --> 18:09.482
A commoner who started out as an orphan 
had the gall to get angry at me!

18:09.482 --> 18:12.122
What's more, he even...

18:12.122 --> 18:13.022
He even...

18:14.402 --> 18:18.532
I swear I won't relent
until I have my revenge!

18:19.022 --> 18:21.532
You're a dead man, Dias!

18:22.312 --> 18:24.432
I'm glad it wasn't anything serious.

18:24.432 --> 18:28.732
Sorry I couldn't keep quiet 
when that arrow grazed my cheek.

18:29.672 --> 18:32.292
If you were listening
 to what I was saying before,

18:32.802 --> 18:37.802
I think you know full well now 
what a foolish thing banditry is!

18:38.072 --> 18:41.172
Except we're mercenaries, not bandits.

18:41.172 --> 18:42.302
Did you say something?!

18:42.302 --> 18:44.802
No, sir, n-not a thing.

18:44.802 --> 18:46.152
Okay.

18:46.632 --> 18:50.962
Then as the lord of this land,
I will now pronounce your punishment!

18:52.402 --> 18:53.582
Your punishment is...

18:58.082 --> 19:01.762
Wasn't kicking them out 
too light a sentence?

19:01.762 --> 19:05.832
No harm done on our side, 
so it felt appropriate.

19:06.142 --> 19:10.632
Although I did lose my cool 
when that arrow grazed you.

19:12.592 --> 19:16.972
Fortunately, we had no casualties, and if
 they learn their lesson, all the better.

19:17.492 --> 19:20.342
If they get up to no good
 in my domain again,

19:21.162 --> 19:24.342
I have no intention of holding back.

19:25.162 --> 19:26.122
All right.

19:26.572 --> 19:30.012
Still, it's a shame one of them got away.

19:30.012 --> 19:32.982
There were so many, 
that's hard to prevent.

19:32.982 --> 19:36.862
Well, I guess we should be 
pleased with such a big haul.

19:37.852 --> 19:41.262
Will these beat-up weapons 
fetch much money?

19:41.912 --> 19:44.682
Steel is precious out on the prairie.

19:44.682 --> 19:47.242
We can melt them down 
to make all sorts of tools.

19:47.612 --> 19:51.582
That's why bandit-hunting 
can turn such a tidy profit.

19:52.462 --> 19:54.872
The chieftain will pay a bounty, too.

19:55.392 --> 19:58.992
My family wasn't exactly
what you'd call well-off.

19:59.722 --> 20:03.202
I would dream of hunting 
scores of bandits like this.

20:04.192 --> 20:08.272
But it's rare that they 
come out to the grasslands.

20:08.672 --> 20:11.732
When I sensed the carriage
 you arrived in,

20:11.732 --> 20:15.272
I was so excited that maybe some
 bandits had finally turned up.

20:15.922 --> 20:20.362
But then it departed immediately, 
leaving just one person.

20:20.812 --> 20:24.902
I figured you'd been abandoned for dead.

20:25.942 --> 20:29.822
The next morning, I came
 to check while I was on patrol,

20:29.822 --> 20:33.622
and I was shocked to find a man sleeping 
there without a care in the world.

20:33.622 --> 20:37.882
I used Soul Appraisal to be safe,
 and your strong blue

20:38.382 --> 20:40.002
really threw me for a loop.

20:40.682 --> 20:45.132
For a moment, I nearly convinced 
myself you were a bandit anyway

20:45.132 --> 20:47.552
so I could kill you and take
 your axe and armor.

20:51.202 --> 20:53.012
I wonder why, though...

20:54.142 --> 20:58.932
I wonder why it occurred to me
 to talk to you instead.

20:59.602 --> 21:04.242
I could've decided killing you was 
extreme and just left you there.

21:06.902 --> 21:10.342
In truth, I can't explain it.

21:10.712 --> 21:12.912
Before I knew it, I was talking to you.

21:14.292 --> 21:20.002
But it got me the life I have now, 
so it wasn't a bad choice.

21:20.642 --> 21:23.502
Still, sometimes, I do wonder...

21:24.042 --> 21:28.882
Why <i>did</i> I choose to speak to you, anyway?

21:32.162 --> 21:35.272
Hey, Alna? What happened?

21:50.622 --> 21:52.512
Uh, Alna...

21:55.622 --> 21:56.642
Wait up!

21:56.642 --> 21:59.242
Alna, don't leave me behind!

22:00.262 --> 22:02.472
<i>I'll chase after her...</i>

22:03.132 --> 22:08.772
<i>because I can only move forward with 
her light parting the darkness for me.</i>
